  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a binary array `nums`, output *the largest number of consecutive* `1`*'s in the array*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,1,0,1,1,1]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: The first two digits or the last three digits are consecutive 1s. The maximum number of consecutive 1s is 3.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,0,1,1,0,1]\nOutput: 2\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 105`\n* `nums[i]` is either `0` or `1`.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
